Marionette AirDrop driver candidate 0038 -- exception-frame contract for
monitor data injection.

Applies on top of 0037 (native/airdrop/driver/0037-monitor-vdev-tx-desc-pool.patch).
File: qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_tx_rx.c

Why
---
0037 gave the monitor vdev a TX descriptor flow pool and the frame finally
reached the firmware, but the firmware answered with a RAMDUMP:

    cnss: MHI status cb is called with reason RDDM(4)
    kiwi_v2: wlan_hdd_pld_uevent: Received firmware hang event
    mhi: device ee: RAMDUMP DOWNLOAD MODE dev_state: SYS ERROR

The only remaining host-side lever on this path is the
struct cdp_tx_exception_metadata, so 0038 asks for the exception-frame
contract instead of a plain vdev-based TCL MSDU.

Effect
------
    metadata.is_tx_sniffer = 1  ->  dp_tx_send_exception() calls
        dp_tx_add_tx_sniffer_meta_data(), which fills an HTT MSDU extension
        header with SEND_AS_STANDALONE + HOST_OPAQUE_VALID and sets
        msdu_info->exception_fw.
    metadata.ppdu_cookie = 1    ->  required by dp_check_exc_metadata() when
        is_tx_sniffer is set; the value is echoed back in the PPDU
        completion, which also gives future candidates a way to observe
        over-the-air completion.

    dp_tx_prepare_desc_single() then prepends that header to the MSDU,
    marks the descriptor TO_FW and routes it through the TQM-bypass WAR,
    and dp_tx_send_msdu_single() sets VALID_HTT in the TCL metadata, so the
    firmware is told the body is a complete host-built frame to send as one
    standalone MSDU rather than something to look up a peer for.

This is the same contract OCB and the mcopy/tx-sniffer paths use, and
is_tx_sniffer/ppdu_cookie are the only two fields the HDD can set here.

Result on device (2026-10-20)
-----------------------------
submitted=1 submitted_bytes=84 rejected=25, and the identical RDDM one frame
after the monitor came up -- the same outcome as 0037.  See 0039 for the
follow-up and native/airdrop/driver/ROADMAP.md section 6.

@@ -774,6 +774,30 @@
 	metadata.tid = 0;
 	metadata.tx_encap_type = htt_cmn_pkt_type_raw;
 	metadata.sec_type = cdp_sec_type_none;
+	/* Marionette: 0037 proved the firmware will not take this frame as a
+	 * regular vdev-based TCL MSDU -- one frame reached it and it went
+	 * straight into RDDM (cnss: MHI status cb is called with reason
+	 * RDDM(4)).  Ask for the exception-frame contract instead.
+	 *
+	 * is_tx_sniffer makes dp_tx_send_exception() call
+	 * dp_tx_add_tx_sniffer_meta_data(), which fills an HTT MSDU extension
+	 * header with SEND_AS_STANDALONE and HOST_OPAQUE_VALID and sets
+	 * msdu_info->exception_fw.  dp_tx_prepare_desc_single() then prepends
+	 * that header and marks the descriptor TO_FW, and
+	 * dp_tx_send_msdu_single() sets VALID_HTT in the TCL metadata, so the
+	 * firmware is told the body is a complete host-built frame to send as
+	 * one standalone MSDU instead of something to search for a peer.
+	 * dp_tx_prepare_htt_metadata() needs no rate or tx-spec input for this
+	 * branch, which matters because a monitor vdev has neither.
+	 *
+	 * dp_check_exc_metadata() requires a non-zero ppdu_cookie when
+	 * is_tx_sniffer is set.  The cookie is echoed back to the host in the
+	 * PPDU completion and is otherwise unused here, so a constant is
+	 * enough.  This is the same contract OCB and the mcopy/tx-sniffer
+	 * paths use, and is_tx_sniffer/ppdu_cookie are the only metadata the
+	 * HDD can set on this path. */
+	metadata.is_tx_sniffer = 1;
+	metadata.ppdu_cookie = 1;
 	skb = cdp_tx_send_exc(soc, adapter->vdev_id, skb, &metadata);
 	if (skb)
 		goto drop;
